{"audio": "romans-14.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 176000, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 1600, "text": "Romans, Chapter Fourteen."}, {"start_ms": 1600, "end_ms": 5867, "text": "Him that is weak in the faith receive ye, but not to doubtful disputations."}, {"start_ms": 5867, "end_ms": 11200, "text": "For one believeth that he may eat all things: another, who is weak, eateth herbs."}, {"start_ms": 11200, "end_ms": 19867, "text": "Let not him that eateth despise him that eateth not; and let not him which eateth not judge him that eateth: for God hath received him."}, {"start_ms": 19867, "end_ms": 22933, "text": "Who art thou that judgest another man's servant?"}, {"start_ms": 22933, "end_ms": 26133, "text": "to his own master he standeth or falleth."}, {"start_ms": 26133, "end_ms": 30267, "text": "Yea, he shall be holden up: for God is able to make him stand."}, {"start_ms": 30267, "end_ms": 35333, "text": "One man esteemeth one day above another: another esteemeth every day alike."}, {"start_ms": 35333, "end_ms": 38667, "text": "Let every man be fully persuaded in his own mind."}, {"start_ms": 38667, "end_ms": 46000, "text": "He that regardeth the day, regardeth it unto the Lord; and he that regardeth not the day, to the Lord he doth not regard it."}, {"start_ms": 46000, "end_ms": 54933, "text": "He that eateth, eateth to the Lord, for he giveth God thanks; and he that eateth not, to the Lord he eateth not, and giveth God thanks."}, {"start_ms": 54933, "end_ms": 59200, "text": "For none of us liveth to himself, and no man dieth to himself."}, {"start_ms": 59200, "end_ms": 68133, "text": "For whether we live, we live unto the Lord; and whether we die, we die unto the Lord: whether we live therefore, or die, we are the Lord's."}, {"start_ms": 68133, "end_ms": 76667, "text": "For to this end Christ both died, and rose, and revived, that he might be Lord both of the dead and living."}, {"start_ms": 76667, "end_ms": 79067, "text": "But why dost thou judge thy brother?"}, {"start_ms": 79067, "end_ms": 81867, "text": "or why dost thou set at nought thy brother?"}, {"start_ms": 81867, "end_ms": 85200, "text": "for we shall all stand before the judgment seat of Christ."}, {"start_ms": 85200, "end_ms": 91600, "text": "For it is written, As I live, saith the Lord, every knee shall bow to me, and every tongue shall confess to God."}, {"start_ms": 91600, "end_ms": 95867, "text": "So then every one of us shall give account of himself to God."}, {"start_ms": 95867, "end_ms": 105600, "text": "Let us not therefore judge one another any more: but judge this rather, that no man put a stumblingblock or an occasion to fall in his brother's way."}, {"start_ms": 105600, "end_ms": 115200, "text": "I know, and am persuaded by the Lord Jesus, that there is nothing unclean of itself: but to him that esteemeth any thing to be unclean, to him it is unclean."}, {"start_ms": 115200, "end_ms": 120000, "text": "But if thy brother be grieved with thy meat, now walkest thou not charitably."}, {"start_ms": 120000, "end_ms": 123333, "text": "Destroy not him with thy meat, for whom Christ died."}, {"start_ms": 123333, "end_ms": 132400, "text": "Let not then your good be evil spoken of: For the kingdom of God is not meat and drink; but righteousness, and peace, and joy in the Holy Ghost."}, {"start_ms": 132400, "end_ms": 137867, "text": "For he that in these things serveth Christ is acceptable to God, and approved of men."}, {"start_ms": 137867, "end_ms": 144400, "text": "Let us therefore follow after the things which make for peace, and things wherewith one may edify another."}, {"start_ms": 144400, "end_ms": 147733, "text": "For meat destroy not the work of God."}, {"start_ms": 147733, "end_ms": 153333, "text": "All things indeed are pure; but it is evil for that man who eateth with offence."}, {"start_ms": 153333, "end_ms": 161600, "text": "It is good neither to eat flesh, nor to drink wine, nor any thing whereby thy brother stumbleth, or is offended, or is made weak."}, {"start_ms": 161600, "end_ms": 162800, "text": "Hast thou faith?"}, {"start_ms": 162800, "end_ms": 165200, "text": "have it to thyself before God."}, {"start_ms": 165200, "end_ms": 169600, "text": "Happy is he that condemneth not himself in that thing which he alloweth."}, {"start_ms": 169600, "end_ms": 176000, "text": "And he that doubteth is damned if he eat, because he eateth not of faith: for whatsoever is not of faith is sin."}], "words": [{"t": "Romans,", "s": 324, "e": 729, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 790, "e": 1094, "si": 0}, {"t": "Fourteen.", "s": 1134, "e": 1580, "si": 0}, {"t": "Him", "s": 1800, "e": 1961, "si": 1}, {"t": "that", "s": 2001, "e": 2121, "si": 1}, {"t": "is", "s": 2161, "e": 2241, "si": 1}, {"t": "weak", "s": 2301, "e": 2481, "si": 1}, {"t": "in", "s": 2542, "e": 2582, "si": 1}, {"t": "the", "s": 2602, "e": 2702, "si": 1}, {"t": "faith", "s": 2722, "e": 3022, "si": 1}, {"t": "receive", "s": 3082, "e": 3483, "si": 1}, {"t": "ye,", "s": 3523, "e": 3603, "si": 1}, {"t": "but", "s": 3804, "e": 3924, "si": 1}, {"t": "not", "s": 3984, "e": 4144, "si": 1}, {"t": "to", "s": 4204, "e": 4284, "si": 1}, {"t": "doubtful", "s": 4385, "e": 4825, "si": 1}, {"t": "disputations.", "s": 4905, "e": 5787, "si": 1}, {"t": "For", "s": 6408, "e": 6529, "si": 2}, {"t": "one", "s": 6649, "e": 6769, "si": 2}, {"t": "believeth", "s": 6809, "e": 7250, "si": 2}, {"t": "that", "s": 7290, "e": 7411, "si": 2}, {"t": "he", "s": 7451, "e": 7511, "si": 2}, {"t": "may", "s": 7591, "e": 7732, "si": 2}, {"t": "eat", "s": 7892, "e": 8032, "si": 2}, {"t": "all", "s": 8153, "e": 8293, "si": 2}, {"t": "things:", "s": 8353, "e": 8774, "si": 2}, {"t": "another,", "s": 9155, "e": 9476, "si": 2}, {"t": "who", "s": 9716, "e": 9817, "si": 2}, {"t": "is", "s": 9877, "e": 9957, "si": 2}, {"t": "weak,", "s": 10037, "e": 10258, "si": 2}, {"t": "eateth", "s": 10458, "e": 10679, "si": 2}, {"t": "herbs.", "s": 10739, "e": 11140, "si": 2}, {"t": "Let", "s": 11821,